cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use solar-and-heliospheric-observatory in your research, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: solar-and-heliospheric-observatory
abstract: >-
  solar-and-heliospheric-observatory is a Python library for downloading and
  analyzing observations from the Solar and Heliospheric Observatory (SOHO),
  starting with the spectra of the Solar Ultraviolet Measurements of Emitted
  Radiation (SUMER) spectrograph. Observations are represented as
  named-arrays function arrays, so a sequence of spectra has named axes and
  physical units, and carries the time, sky position, and wavelength of every
  pixel.
authors:
  - family-names: Smart
    given-names: Roy T.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9997-5515"
repository-code: "https://github.com/sun-data/solar-and-heliospheric-observatory"
url: "https://solar-and-heliospheric-observatory.readthedocs.io"
license: BSD-3-Clause
keywords:
  - SOHO
  - SUMER
  - solar physics
  - data access
